2. Information We May Collect Automatically
When you use our services, we may automatically collect certain information, primarily including the following:
Information Type
Specific Information
Data Processing Activities and Explanations
Account Information
Account ID (generated when users register)
Manage your information and account.
Location Data
The approximate geographic location of the device, inferred from the IP address, such as at the country or city level.
Note: We do not collect precise GPS location information.
1) Provide services (such as offering age-appropriate content or language versions based on your region);
2) Operate, provide, maintain, protect, manage, and customize our apps and how they are provided;
3) Improve the app experience and identify fraud, security, or technical issues related to the apps (such as detecting logins from unusual locations).
Technical Data
1) IP address;
2) Device operating system version, device model, device brand, device resolution, device language, device identifier (OpenUDID, collected on iOS only);
3) App ID (Application ID/Bundle ID): Used to identify the app's runtime environment and version updates;
4) App Set ID/App Group ID: Used for basic cross-app statistical analysis and fraud prevention;
5) Advertising ID (IDFA): Collected only on iOS devices and used solely for behaviorally targeted advertising with user consent, ad frequency control and basic attribution analysis; not collected from children;
6) Cookies: Used only for web-based services (for adults) to maintain login status and perform basic statistical analysis; we do not use cookies for cross-site tracking or behavioral marketing.
1) Ensure the proper operation and compatibility of our apps;
2) Analyze app performance and troubleshoot technical issues;
3) Prevent fraud and maintain security;
4) Not used for behavioral advertising targeted at children, profiling, or automated decision-making.
Regarding cookie management, you can control cookies through your device's system settings or the cookie banners displayed in our apps, where you can choose to accept or reject non-essential cookies.
Log and Usage Data
1) Frequency and duration of app usage;
2) Features used and actions performed within the apps, including browsing and tapping behavior;
3) In-app progress, in-app purchases (excluding financial data such as bank account and credit card information), aggregated usage statistics, and performance data;
4) Error and crash reports.
1) Improve and optimize app features and the user experience;
2) Troubleshoot issues and ensure stable service operation;
3) Conduct aggregated statistical analysis to understand user trends (without identifying individuals);
4) Crash logs will also be used for security incident investigations and verification of fixes.

1. Age Confirmation and Parental Consent Mechanism
We take children's privacy seriously. When users access our services, if they indicate during registration or at key points of operation that they are below the applicable legal age threshold for "children", we will:
(1) Restrict data collection: By default, disable behavioral tracking and personalized advertising features;
(2) Obtain parental consent: Require the provision of a parent's or legal guardian's email address and send a parental consent form (Verifiable Parental Consent) to explain the types of data we will collect and the purposes for which such data will be used;
(3) Confirm consent: The parent or legal guardian must confirm consent by replying to the email. Before obtaining such consent, we will not collect any children's personal data beyond what is permitted by applicable laws (except for technical data necessary for internal operations, such as crash logs).

1. We will store information on servers located closest to the end user in order to provide secure and fast services. The server locations include:
（1）The United States;
（2）Hong Kong;
（3）Germany.
You acknowledge and agree that your data may be processed on our servers or the servers of our processors, which may be located outside your country of residence. Nevertheless, we will ensure that appropriate measures are implemented to protect your personal data in accordance with this Privacy Policy. This means that all of our service providers and partners are required to process personal data in compliance with the European Union's General Data Protection Regulation ("GDPR") and other applicable laws.
